Data
"How Apple Is Organized for Innovation" is an HBR reprint (R2006F), provided for personal use only, so it is not redistributed here. Obtain your own copy and update the path in the notebook:

pdf_path = "/content/drive/MyDrive/Apple HBR Report Project/HBR_How_Apple_Is_Organized_For_Innovation.pdf"
Setup
Library versions used:

langchain==0.3.27 langchain_community==0.3.27 chromadb==1.0.15 pymupdf==1.26.3 tiktoken==0.9.0 datasets==4.0.0 evaluate==0.4.5 langchain_openai==0.3.30
Create a config.json in the project folder:

{ "OPENAI_API_KEY": "your_key_here", "OPENAI_API_BASE": "https://api.openai.com/v1" }
Then run the notebook cells in order.

Before you upload

API key: never commit config.json. Add this to a .gitignore file in the repo: config.json apple_hbr_chroma_db/
Notebook output: clear any saved output that shows your key. Your notebook prompts for it with getpass, but check the saved file.
PDF: leave it out of a public repo. The README already says why.
Placeholders: replace the two file names in "Files".
Requirements file: if you'd rather use a requirements.txt, the version block under "Setup" works as its contents.
